{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the scalar local limit theorem with corrected stable norming (Theorem 1.10), the admissible leaf counts and their probability asymptotics (Theorem 3.1, Introduction (I)), maximum degree concentration under the paper's hypothesis H (Theorem 7.1(ii)), and corrected probability asymptotics for the number of vertices with degree in an arbitrary set (Theorem 8.1(I)). The principal functional results are the joint convergence of the rescaled Lukasiewicz path, contour and height under leaf conditioning (Introduction (II), including lattice laws) and under offspring-mark conditioning (Theorem 8.1(II)). Nine principal declarations and their explicit construction lemmas are selected for comparison. Tree laws, codings and limit laws are concrete; evaluation and J1 metric instances are fixed by checked characterizations.",
